y-500","children":"130 km"}]]}],["$","a","Multan",{"href":"/pakistan/punjab/multan","className":"bg-[#F5F3EE] hover:bg-green-50 rounded-xl p-4 flex justify-between items-center transition","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"font-medium text-gray-800","children":"Multan"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"text-xs text-gray-500","children":"340 km"}]]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed text-sm","children":"karachi's strategic location in central Punjab places it within easy reach of several major Pakistani cities in June 2026. Islamabad and Rawalpindi — Pakistan's capital twin cities — are just 280 km north via the M-2 Motorway, a journey of approximately 3.5 hours by car or under 4 hours by Daewoo Express bus. Gujranwala, Pakistan's fourth-largest city and a major industrial centre, is only 80 km northeast of karachi. Faisalabad, the country's textile capital, lies 130 km to the west. Sialkot, renowned for its sports goods manufacturing, is 130 km east. Multan, the City of Saints, is 340 km south — a roughly 4-hour drive. This central position makes karachi a natural hub for trade, travel, and cultural exchange across Punjab. The Lahore-Islamabad Motorway (M-2), the Ring Road, and the expanding Orange Line Metro system have all dramatically improved connectivity in and around karachi in recent years."}]]}]
